  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is even and it is an even number\" to just \"$x$ is even.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is even, or $x$ is even or it divides $11.$\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$x$ is even or $x$ is even, or it divides $11.$\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is even or $x$ is even\" to just \"$x$ is even.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is even, or it divides $11.$\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$x$ is even or it divides $11.$\"",
